{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06GV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: R \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathfrak m_R/\\mathfrak m_R^2 \\to \\mathfrak m_S/\\mathfrak m_S^2$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathfrak m_R/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda R + \\mathfrak m_R^2) \\to\n\\mathfrak m_S/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda S + \\mathfrak m_S^2)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-surjective-cotangent-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cc0d83e1a0e551334f9813f2c6a44cc481d84732a8849cb9f6dc9563a9a41245", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d779f8e9ebca1721d94c7aa34ad6edd81d7e14430f96a03159e7c1d80b56cf39", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map in <MATH_0002>.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is surjective,\n<STRUCT_0003> the map\n<MATH_0004>\nis surjective, and\n<STRUCT_0004> the map\n<MATH_0005>\nis surjective.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:26858627d14ee4d81754444a5b07f919eac1ab007711f36869cda4635c3929de", "unit_id": "tag:06GZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06GV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$n \\geq 2$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\mathfrak m_R/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda R + \\mathfrak m_R^2)\n=\n\\mathfrak m_{R_n}/(\\mathfrak m_\\Lambda R_n + \\mathfrak m_{R_n}^2)\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$R_n \\to S_n$", "MATH_0005": "$n$", "MATH_0006": "$K_n$", "MATH_0007": "$R_n \\to S_n$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n0 \\to K_n \\to R_n \\to S_n \\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$(K_n)$", "MATH_0010": "$K_n$", "MATH_0011": "$\\lim R_n \\to \\lim S_n$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-surjective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-ML-exact-sequence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:80c4f4851c8a8557e1d0d90beaade6b63ce79e85fc0a89cf74330805b231f2c8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7bc67a70190a7b29b9b24fda6a1b7a6f56490624f0fd2a5a4440cb69bd9ee472", "source_text": "Note that for <MATH_0001> we have the equality of relative cotangent spaces\n<MATH_0002>\nand similarly for <MATH_0003>. Hence by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that <MATH_0004> is surjective for all <MATH_0005>.\nNow let <MATH_0006> be the kernel of <MATH_0007>.  Then the sequences\n<MATH_0008>\nform an exact sequence of directed inverse systems. The system <MATH_0009> is\nMittag-Leffler since each <MATH_0010> is Artinian. Hence by\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>\ntaking limits preserves exactness. So\n<MATH_0011> is surjective, i.e., <MATH_0012> is surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:31ecf157d34cb3d4d2b6dd80dcf1a5d5e982606c240d65272508df32f16b8ef9", "unit_id": "tag:06GZ:proof"}
